While 60ms might seem negligible in a web request, at scale (thousands of concurrent requests or tight loops), this overhead accumulates significantly. Furthermore, LINQ creates additional memory allocations (predicates, enumerators, intermediate lists) that trigger more frequent Garbage Collection (GC) pressure.

