## Advanced Optimization Strategies

### 1. Use `Span<T>` and `Memory<T>` for Zero-Allocation Filtering
```csharp
public void FilterWithSpan(int[] source, Span<int> destination)
{
    int destIndex = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < source.Length; i++)
    {
        if (source[i] > 0)
        {
            if (destIndex < destination.Length)
                destination[destIndex++] = source[i];
            else
                break; // Destination full
        }
    }
}
```

### 2. Parallel Processing for Multi-Core CPUs
```csharp
public List<int> FilterInParallel(List<int> source)
{
    var partitions = Partitioner.Create(source).GetPartitions(Environment.ProcessorCount);
    var results = new List<List<int>>(Environment.ProcessorCount);

    Parallel.ForEach(partitions, partition =>
    {
        var localResult = new List<int>();
        while (partition.MoveNext())
        {
            if (partition.Current > 0)
                localResult.Add(partition.Current);
        }
        results.Add(localResult);
    });

    // Merge results (this step is fast compared to filtering)
    var merged = new List<int>();
    foreach (var result in results)
        merged.AddRange(result);

    return merged;
}
```

