| Method Complexity | Estimated JIT Overhead (First Call) |
| :--- | :--- |
| Simple | 1–5 µs |
| Moderate | 10–100 µs |
| Complex | 100–500+ µs |

In modern .NET with **Tiered Compilation**, the first-call penalty is often at the lower end of these ranges because Tier 0 JIT is very fast. The "real" optimization happens in the background and doesn’t block your code.

