while ($html =~ /<a\b[^>]*?href\s*=\s*["']([^"']*)["']/gsi) {
    push @links, $1;
}
```

**Changes from your original:**
1. `<a\b` instead of `<a\s+` — handles `<ahref="..."` (edge case) and `<a href="..."` (standard)
2. `[^>]*?` (non-greedy) instead of `[^>]*` — minimal performance gain, but safer
3. `["']` handles both single and double quotes
4. `/s` flag makes `.` match newlines (not needed here but good habit)
5. `/i` flag for case-insensitivity (`<A>`, `<a>`, etc.)
6. **Loop form** instead of list assignment avoids creating a massive intermediate list

### If Your HTML Might Be Malformed (Production-Safe)

