gcc -O3 -march=native -o matmul_o3 matrix_mult.cpp
```

> **Important**: Use `-march=native` so the compiler knows your CPU's SIMD capabilities (AVX2, AVX-512, etc.). Without it, GCC may default to SSE2 (128-bit), drastically reducing vectorization benefits regardless of optimization level.

