## Benchmark 2: Matrix Multiplication (100×100 Matrices)

This is a more realistic CPU-intensive task. Matrix multiplication is O(n³) = 1,000,000 multiplications-additions for 100×100.

### Optimized JS Implementation (3-loop, flat arrays)
```javascript
function matMulJS(a, b, n) {
    const c = new Float64Array(n * n);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            let sum = 0;
            for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                sum += a[i * n + k] * b[k * n + j];
            }
            c[i * n + j] = sum;
        }
    }
    return c;
}
```

### C++ Implementation (compiled to Wasm, with `-O3 -ffast-math`)
```cpp
void matMulWasm(const double* a, const double* b, double* c, int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            double sum = 0;
            for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                sum += a[i * n + k] * b[k * n + j];
            }
            c[i * n + j] = sum;
        }
    }
}
```

