    }
}

$tree->delete; # Free memory
```

#### Option 2: HTML::Parser (Speed & Low Memory for Large Files) ✅ **Recommended for Large Files**
`HTML::Parser` is an event-based parser. It does **not** load the entire DOM into memory. It processes the file sequentially, so it scales to gigabytes.

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use HTML::Parser;

my $parser = HTML::Parser->new(
    api_version => 3,
    start_h => [ sub {
        my ($tag, $attr, $orig) = @_;
