## How Method Complexity Affects JIT Time

| Method Complexity | JIT Time (μs) | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Trivial** (getter/setter) | ~1–3 μs | `public int GetX() => x;` |
| **Simple** (few ops) | ~3–10 μs | Arithmetic, single branch |
| **Moderate** (loops, branching) | ~10–30 μs | The `Compute` method above |
| **Complex** (deep recursion, generic instantiation, large IL) | ~30–100+ μs | Heavy LINQ chains, complex generics |
| **Very Complex** (micro-generator-like IL) | ~100–500+ μs | Dynamically generated IL, large switch statements |

