### 📊 General Performance Expectations (Random Data, ~14k elements)

| Algorithm          | Best Case     | Avg Case      | Worst Case    | Practical Notes                          |
|--------------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|------------------------------------------|
| **Timsort**        | O(n)          | O(n log n)    | O(n log n)    | Excellent stability, low overhead in interpreted languages |
| **Dual-Pivot Quicksort** | O(n log n) | O(n log n)    | O(n²)         | Fast in compiled languages, but worst-case rare with good pivot selection |
| **Introsort** (C++)| O(n log n)    | O(n log n)    | O(n log n)    | Hybest of both: starts as Quicksort, falls back to Heapsort |

