## Optimized C++ Implementation (Using simdjson)

`simdjson` is one of the fastest JSON parsers in existence, using SIMD instructions for validation and parsing.

```cpp
// benchmark.cpp
#include <simdjson.h>
#include <chrono>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

// Parse JSON and extract specific fields without unnecessary allocations
struct ParsedData {
  std::string id;
  double value;
  std::string timestamp;
};

std::vector<ParsedData> parse_json(const simdjson::dom::object& root) {
  std::vector<ParsedData> results;
  auto items = root["items"].get_array();
  for (auto& item : items) {
    ParsedData data;
    item["id"].get_string().get(data.id);
    item["value"].get_double().get(data.value);
    item["timestamp"].get_string().get(data.timestamp);
    results.push_back(std::move(data));
  }
  return results;
}

