**Use `HTML::LinkExtor`**. It's:
- Part of Perl's core distribution (no extra installs needed)
- Battle-tested on decades of real-world HTML
- Memory-efficient when combined with line-by-line reading
- Correct by design

If you're processing **terabytes** of data, consider using `HTML::TreeBuilder`'s sibling `HTML::TagAngler` or even a dedicated tool like [`hxselect`](https://github.com/cataphora/hxselect) or [`ripgrepper`](https://github.com/... ) for ultra-high-throughput scenarios.

