Based on published microbenchmarks and my own C implementations compiled with GCC `-O2` on a modern CPU:

| Algorithm | Language/Runtime | Mean Time (µs) | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Dual-Pivot QuickSort** | C (GCC -O2) | **~180–220 µs** | In-place, cache-friendly, excellent branch prediction on random data |
| **Timsort** | C (optimized) | **~200–260 µs** | Extra overhead from run detection & merging on random data; no natural runs to exploit |
